    "summary": "Smokin' Oakland ’82 – fire‑filled Scarlet Begonias>Fire & a monster Black Peter",
    "review": "The December 27, 1982 show at the Oakland Auditorium Arena is one of those late‑year gems that still feels fresh. The band rides a high‑energy groove from the opening “Bertha” through a tightly woven first set, then launches into an all‑time great second set where the Scarlet Begonias → Fire on the Mountain segue erupts into tribal drums and a relentless drive. Jerry’s solos are described as fully committed with a perfect tone, and Brent’s keyboards add intricate, splashy color that locks in with Bob’s vocal fire (“wailing Donna back into the stone age”). Highlights include a soaring “Black Peter,” an inspired “The Wheel” into a uniquely puzzling but ultimately effective transition to “The Other One,” and a rousing “Sugar Magnolia” that caps the set. While a few moments (a hurried “Playing In The Band”) dip, the overall momentum stays high, making this a must‑listen for any Deadhead looking for a late‑’80s showcase of tight playing and classic improvisation.",
